# TaskFlow — Full-Stack Task Management App

## 1. Project Overview

TaskFlow is a modern, responsive task management web application that allows users to organize daily tasks, track progress, and manage completed and pending work.

The project includes a complete frontend, backend REST API, and database.

The goal is to build a functional application with clean UI, reusable components, maintainable code, and a well-organized architecture.

## 2. Technology Stack

### Frontend

* React
* TypeScript
* Vite
* Tailwind CSS
* React Router
* Axios
* Lucide React icons

### Backend

* Node.js
* Express.js
* TypeScript
* Zod for request validation

### Database

* PostgreSQL
* Prisma ORM

### Testing

* Vitest
* React Testing Library
* Supertest

## 3. Main Features

### Dashboard

* Display total tasks.
* Display pending tasks.
* Display completed tasks.
* Show recent tasks.
* Show task completion statistics.

### Task Management

* Create a new task.
* View all tasks.
* View individual task details.
* Edit task titles and descriptions.
* Change task status.
* Set task priority.
* Set due dates.
* Delete tasks.
* Search tasks by title.
* Filter tasks by status and priority.
* Sort tasks by creation date or due date.

### User Interface

* Responsive sidebar navigation.
* Dashboard overview cards.
* Task list with status indicators.
* Create and edit task forms.
* Confirmation dialog before deleting tasks.
* Loading indicators.
* Empty states.
* Error messages and success notifications.
* Responsive layouts for desktop, tablet, and mobile.

## 4. Task Data Model

Each task should contain:

* `id`: Unique identifier.
* `title`: Task title.
* `description`: Optional task description.
* `status`: `PENDING`, `IN_PROGRESS`, or `COMPLETED`.
* `priority`: `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, or `HIGH`.
* `dueDate`: Optional due date.
* `createdAt`: Creation timestamp.
* `updatedAt`: Last update timestamp.

Use PostgreSQL with Prisma to define the schema and manage database operations.

## 5. API Endpoints

Create the following REST API endpoints.

| Method | Endpoint                | Description                     |
| ------ | ----------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/api/health`           | Check server status             |
| GET    | `/api/tasks`            | Get tasks with optional filters |
| GET    | `/api/tasks/:id`        | Get one task                    |
| POST   | `/api/tasks`            | Create a task                   |
| PUT    | `/api/tasks/:id`        | Update a task                   |
| PATCH  | `/api/tasks/:id/status` | Update task status              |
| DELETE | `/api/tasks/:id`        | Delete a task                   |
| GET    | `/api/dashboard/stats`  | Get dashboard statistics        |

Support query parameters for searching, filtering, sorting, and pagination where appropriate.

Validate all incoming requests and return consistent JSON responses with appropriate HTTP status codes.

## 6. Frontend Pages

### Dashboard

Show task statistics, completion progress, and recently updated tasks.

### All Tasks

Show a searchable, filterable, and sortable task list.

### Create Task

Provide a form to create a task with a title, description, priority, and due date.

### Edit Task

Allow users to update existing task information.

### Task Details

Show complete task information and provide actions to edit, complete, or delete the task.

### Not Found

Show a friendly page when a route does not exist.

